articles/c6eq84eygz0qo--d4807c8344ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq84eygz0qo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The man was beaten with hammers until he transferred hundreds of thousands of pounds of cryptocurrency.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump's AI rebrand causes 'unprecedented' demand for Slovenian website names</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2z23xj555o#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:37:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2z23xj555o--9db916080857.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2z23xj555o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The president wants AI to be called super intelligence - or SI - the same initials used by Slovenian domains.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI boom could trigger market shocks, Bank of England boss warns</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8e30enrkxyo#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:05:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8e30enrkxyo--df6ead8af4b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8e30enrkxyo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Andrew Bailey says the central bank is watching the waves of cash being invested in artificial intelligence "very carefully".</summary></entry><entry><title>Tiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon photo contest</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck4gjn1yzprno#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:10:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck4gjn1yzprno--a55a8a4a0acb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck4gjn1yzprno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Dr Ning Xu denies he broke the rules of Nikon's annual Small World In Motion contest.</summary></entry><entry><title>The AI telling farmers when to harvest</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgk53dkmyxko#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgk53dkmyxko--b63e79dbf28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgk53dkmyxko?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Will farmers want AI tools to help judge when to pick fruit, or is their own intuition enough?</summary></entry><entry><title>Regulating AI 'not the right place to start' says Bailey</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvzez7k0pn40o#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:00:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvzez7k0pn40o--e200963ec8d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvzez7k0pn40o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI needs "rigorous" testing and safeguards to contain risk, Andrew Bailey says.</summary></entry><entry><title>WhatsApp introduces optional parental controls for teenagers</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm986x65we88o#0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm986x65we88o--a64ee96133a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm986x65we88o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The social messaging app will let parents decide on privacy settings for their child's account.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI unveils AI assistant 'dots' while safety worries delay new model</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news